 "answer": {
  "answer": "The study confirmed 4 of the 5 challenging settings it was asked for, each on a different scene. It did not find a fifth. On 09a95ffa (cars 1 s earlier at 1.5x speed), 023b7fcc (0.5 s earlier at recorded speed) and 0e899dd3 (recorded timing at 2x speed), every run failed. In each of them the policy drifted left out of its lane against a RIGHT or STRAIGHT command and hit a car in the next lane. On 096988dd (0.5 s earlier at 2x speed), every run also failed, but by rear-ending a lead car that the camera showed as a smeared blob, so the simulator's rendering may explain those failures. All 09a95ffa failures were also flagged as possible artifacts, because the ego ended more than 3.5 m off the recorded path. Each confirmed case rests on four or five repeats, so its 90% range is only known to sit above one half. Without baseline runs with traffic replayed as recorded, it is not shown how much of the leftward drift the retiming causes.",
